    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 60 tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`), including the new `Cp14Tests` and `Cp48Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI moved the owner's date-derived values onto a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year runs 1 July \u2013 30 June, named by the calendar year in which it ends \u2014 the Australian convention matching this app's NSW/VIC/QLD regions).\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`**\n- Added `fiscalYearOf(LocalDate)` \u2014 the fiscal year a date falls in (`month \u2265 July \u2192 year+1`, else `year`).\n- Added `fiscalYear(Owner)` \u2014 returns `FY<YY>` from the business-day-adjusted `registrationDate` (already rolled forward in `BuildOwner`), or `null` for seed data with no registration date. Wired it into `toOwnerDto` via a new `@Mapping`.\n- `membershipNumber(Owner)` \u2014 the `-M<YY>` segment now uses the fiscal year instead of the calendar year, so its `YY` always matches `fiscalYear`'s.\n- `membershipPoints(Owner)` \u2014 the tenure bonus (+3) now triggers on elapsed fiscal years (`fiscalYearOf(now) \u2212 fiscalYearOf(registration) > 1`) rather than a 365-day window. A new owner still has zero tenure, so it never earns the bonus (the invariant the existing point/level tests rely on).\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `fiscalYear` property (`FY<YY>`) to the `Owner` schema, updated `membershipNumber`'s description/example (`M27`) to reference the fiscal year, and updated the `membershipPoints` tenure wording. The `OwnerDto` is generated from this spec at build time, so the new field flows through automatically. The audit line (`AuditOwnerCreated`) uses the mapper's `membershipNumber`, so it stays consistent.\n\nOne deliberate interpretation worth flagging: the spec didn't pin the exact tenure threshold, so I translated \"tenure exceeds 365 days\" (~more than one year) to \"elapsed fiscal years > 1\", which aligns with the old boundary at the exactly-one-year mark. No test distinguishes this since all point-scoring tests use fresh owners.",
